  "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 12-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: ZnSe / ZnS / ZnSe / ZnS / ZnSe / ZnS / ZnSe / ZnS / ZnSe / ZnS / ZnSe / ZnS. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Execute coherent TMM optimization for a 12-layer ZnS/ZnSe dielectric stack on Ge substrate at normal incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS|ZnSe|ZnS|ZnSe|ZnS|ZnSe|ZnS|ZnSe|ZnS|ZnSe|ZnS|ZnSe (12 finite layers). Freeze layers 1, 2, 11, 12 at quarter-wave optical thickness centered at 4000 nm (MWIR band center). Optimize thicknesses of layers 3-10 (8 central layers) with bounds 500-1000 nm. Wavelength bands: 8000-11000 nm (high transmittance target), 3000-5000 nm (low transmittance target). Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 100 iterations. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
